! mcp_bootstrap_p151.strap -- "R E A D", printed page 151.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.158.  Header read and not
! assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11011MCP   CARD ID IA000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE
! NUMBER 151".
!
! >>> THE HEADING ROW'S OWN LOCATION FIELD IS BLANK. <<<  The
! column-heading line prints "LINE  LOCATION  BINARY OUTPUT  NAME
! STATEMENT  LOCATION" and NOTHING follows that second LOCATION --
! rendered at 900 dpi and looked at, not guessed.  So this page
! joins printed pp.83, 144 and 145 in omitting the origin word,
! and no digits are recorded here.  (A BLANK is not a zero; see
! docs/transcription_workflow.md step 1.)  It also kills, again,
! the tempting "the field is dropped on pages carrying their own
! SLC" story only in one direction: this page DOES carry an SLC
! and DOES omit the field, which is consistent with that guess,
! while pp.133/136/138/139/141/142/143 are the pages that refuted
! it.  Nothing new is claimed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Forty-eight printed lines, all of them code or banner.  No SYN,
! no DD, no VF, no DR/DRZ, no data of any kind -- so rule 5 of
! "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" (DR vs DRZ) does not arise here.
!
!   lines 1-3   the asterisk box around the heading
!               "***************** R E A D *****************"
!   line  4     "SLC,$"
!   lines 5-48  forty-four instructions, every one of them CODE.
!
! The routine is the MCP READ setup.  C22-6728 (MCP System
! Analysis Guide), a TYPESET manual and therefore a genuinely
! independent press, describes this exact code twice:
!
!   "The control word check routine (Figure 99) is entered with
!    the calling sequence SIC, B1RA; B, BCWCR, with the location
!    of the first control word in the VF of $0."
!                                          -- C22-6728, PDF p.177
!
! which is lines 5 and 6 VERBATIM, and
!
!   "It is entered at ZSTEVL with the location of a status
!    evaluation mask in SEVLMK in the unit area table, and the
!    first location of a table of branch instructions in SEVLTB
!    in the unit area table."                  -- same page
!
! which is lines 7-11 and the ZSTEVL branches on lines 15 and 21.
!
! The body is:
!   Z START (5)   SIC/B into the control-word check (B CWCR).
!   7-11          plant Z EVL MK in S EVL MK and K FORK in
!                 S EVL TB, i.e. set up the status evaluation to
!                 come back to this page's own K FORK, and set
!                 S CH OP to say the channel is operating.
!   12            "BR,0.0($4)" -- branch into the sixteen-entry
!                 equipment table on $4.
!   13-28         the table: 0 illegal, 1 disk, 2 console, 3 card
!                 reader, 4-7 incorrect/no equipment, 10 tape,
!                 11-17 no equipment.  Sixteen half-word branches,
!                 one per equipment code, exactly as the comment
!                 column numbers them 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,10,11..17.
!   K FORK (29)   where the status evaluation returns: dispatch on
!                 the unit -- K K LOC, R VFY, P CSRD -- then
!                 KVI,4,4.0 "-TEST IF TAPE", BZXE to K YOME if
!                 console, and the file-count / label-mode tests.
!   K TEST M (38) set the channel to file mode, or label mode if
!                 the IOD is null; SIC/B to K MODE to check the
!                 mode selected.
!   K YOME (43)   "SETUP READ OPERATION" (the manual's own words
!                 for this box, Figure 99): pick up the control
!                 word address, plant the live RD at K GO+.32,
!                 CNOP, LX/SX the instruction into S IO INS, and
!   K GO (48)     issue it -- "RD,0.0($14),0  -ISSUE RD COMMAND".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FORTY-FIVE CARDS OVER FORTY-EIGHT LINES; NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER
! END
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! COUNTED OFF THE CARD-SERIAL COLUMN, not off the survey.  The
! serials run IA000001 (line 1) to IA000045 (line 48) with no gap,
! and three serials are printed TWICE, on two statements each:
!
!   IA000036  lines 36 and 37   SIC,S SCRPM($12) + B,RS1 FLK
!   IA000040  lines 41 and 42   SIC,K K MODE     + B,K MODE
!   IA000044  lines 46 and 47   LX,0,$+1.0       + SX,0,S IO INS
!
! 45 + 3 = 48, so every printed line is accounted for and the
! render lost nothing.  Line 1 is the page's first line (the
! render starts at y=480 at 400 dpi, which is LINE 1) and line 48
! is followed by blank paper to the bottom rule.
!
! >>> WHERE THIS DECK DISAGREES WITH THE SURVEY. <<<  The survey
! reported 34 rows spanning 217544.0..217567.0.  This page has 46
! emitting HALF WORDS over 44 statements and runs
! 217544.00..217572.40.  The survey lost the whole tail from line
! 44 on -- the SVA/CNOP/LX/SX/RD that are the point of the routine
! -- and under-read the middle.  The deck wins because every one
! of the 46 half words is checked against the printed BINARY
! OUTPUT column below, and all 46 agree.
!
! NOTE THE CARD-PAIR ASYMMETRY, recorded because it is printed:
! lines 5 and 6 are ALSO a SIC/branch pair and they carry TWO
! serials (IA000005, IA000006), while the SIC/branch pairs on
! 36/37 and 41/42 each carry one.  So "a SIC and its branch share
! a card" is NOT a rule on this page.  Nothing here depends on it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 4 PRINTS "217544.00   SLC,$" AND THAT IS A FREE WITNESS.
! An SLC emits nothing, so its printed LOCATION *is* the counter
! arriving from printed p.150.  This deck writes a hard
! "SLC,(8)217544.0" so it assembles standalone, which ASSERTS the
! origin rather than checking it (docs/transcription_workflow.md,
! "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE ARRIVING COUNTER"), so the
! printed value is recorded here and in the first !CHECK note.
!
! NEAR SIDE, and it closes: the volume OCR of printed p.150 (a
! legitimate index onto ANOTHER page) ends at its line 28,
! "217531.00 *  000013.00   AEDMPB  DRZ(..),(11)" -- the OCR
! garbles the name and the operand ("MPR ORZINDODD") but prints
! the LOCATION and the RESERVATION COUNT cleanly, and p.150's own
! lines 26 and 27 are "AEDMPI XW,AEDMPB,6" and "AEDMPA
! XW,AEDMPB,6" both resolving to 217531.00+, which independently
! fixes that card's address.  A reservation prints its COUNT in
! the BINARY OUTPUT column, so 000013.00 is 0o13 = eleven words,
! and 0o217531 + 0o13 = 0o217544 EXACTLY.  The counter leaves
! p.150 at 217544.00, which is what line 4 here prints.  (What
! carries this is the ARITHMETIC off two clean octal fields, not
! the OCR's reading of any name.)
!
! FAR SIDE, independent of this page: the volume OCR carries, on a
! page near 220744, "220744.40  217544.10 00   B,Z START  -READ".
! A plain B prints target+.10, so Z START is at 217544.00 -- this
! page's first label, read off a DIFFERENT printed page.
!
! So the near side is a measurement, not a prediction; what is
! left for the p.150 transcriber is only to confirm that its line
! 28 really is an eleven-word reservation at 217531.00.
!
! >>> PREDICTION FOR THE p.152 TRANSCRIBER: line 48 is a FULL WORD
!     at 217572.00, so the counter leaves this page at 217573.00.
!     p.152's first emitting row should print 217573.00.  (If
!     p.152 opens with its own "SLC,$" its printed LOCATION should
!     read 217573.00 and that settles it outright.) <<<
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS -- WHAT WAS SETTLED AND ON WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page opens round glyphs constantly.  ITS OWN COLUMN HEADING
! PRINTS "LCCATICN" for LOCATION, which is the cleanest possible
! calibration: in that one word the drum prints two known O's as
! broken-right C-shapes right beside a known C.  Every LOCATION
! field prints "217544.CC" for .00, and every octal BINARY field
! likewise, so a round glyph in a LOCATION or in an octal BINARY
! field is a 0 with certainty (C is not an octal digit).  The
! glyphs that are NOT in an octal field were each settled on
! something else, and ink varies per CHARACTER here, so the
! calibration licenses nothing by itself.
!
! (1) >>> THE TYPESET MANUAL SETTLED THE NAMES, AND IT IS THE
!     STRONGEST EVIDENCE ON THIS PAGE. <<<  C22-6728 and
!     C22-6728-1 (MCP System Analysis Guide) are a different
!     press, different ink, and genuinely independent of this
!     drum.  Counting hits across the two revisions:
!
!       ZSTART 4/4   KILEGL 13/17   ZDISK1 3/3   ZSTEVL 15/17
!       RVFY   8/9   PCSRD   8/7    KKLOC 14/16  KKMODE 1/1
!       KTESTM 3/2   KGO     1/2    KMODE  4/3   RS1FLK 1/0
!       B1RA   2/0   BCWCR   4/4    KYOME  1/0
!       SEVLMK 6/6   SEVLTB  7/7    SCHOP  5/8   SIOINS 5/5
!       SSCRPM 4/4   SLABM   1/1    SFILEK 5/5   SFMODE 1/1
!       SCWADR 2/2
!
!     TWENTY-FOUR of this page's TWENTY-SIX distinct symbol names
!     are confirmed letter-for-letter by a typeset source.  The
!     only two that are not are K FORK and Z EVL MK, and both are
!     written up below.  In particular:
!
!     * "K YOME" (lines 33 and 43).  On the drum the middle glyph
!       is the usual broken-right round shape and the name is not
!       an English word, so neither the comment column nor shape
!       could settle it; the volume OCR carries only this page's
!       own two cards, which is not a witness.  SETTLED BY
!       RENDERING C22-6728 PDF p.167 AT 900 dpi: "Figure 90 - The
!       Read Routine" is a flowchart of THIS VERY PAGE, and its
!       box reads "KYOME / SET UP READ OPERATION. STORE IN SIOINS
!       IN UAT" with a FULLY CLOSED O.  The argument is the
!       dropout asymmetry, and the figure supplies its own
!       calibration: that chart's printer drops O's constantly --
!       in the SAME figure KMODE prints "KMCCE", KKLOC prints
!       "KKLCC", KGO prints "KGC", S CH OP prints "SCHCP" and
!       CONSOLE prints "CCNSCLE" -- yet KYOME's O came out closed.
!       Ink can open a closed glyph and never closes an open one,
!       so an observed O is not a damaged C.  O, decisively.
!       Figure 90 also corroborates the whole routine
!       independently: ZSTART -> BCWCR "CW ADDRESS CHECKING" ->
!       the tape/console/disk/card-reader dispatch -> ZSTEVL,
!       ZDISK1, KILEGL, KTESTM, RS1FLK "SPACE OVER LABEL TAPE
!       MARK", KMODE "CHECK FOR PROPER MODE SELECTED", KYOME,
!       KGO "READ", and KKLOC "LOCATE ARC".
!     * "RS1 FLK" (line 37).  Digit 1, not letter I: the manual
!       prints RS1FLK, and the DEFINING card on another printed
!       page (volume OCR, 220143.00, "RS1 FLK BZB,S SYSTM($12),
!       K N SYST") spells it the same way.
!     * "B IRA" (line 5).  Letter I, not digit 1: the manual's
!       prose prints it BOTH ways across its two revisions -- see
!       the B1RA note below; the ink settles it, not the manual.
!     * "P CSRD" (line 31) ends in D, not O -- the C/D pair this
!       drum breaks worst.  Confirmed twice over: the manual
!       prints PCSRD, and decks/mcp_bootstrap_p138.strap DEFINES
!       the label PCSRD at 217071.00, which is exactly the address
!       line 31 branches to.
!
! (2) "K FORK" (lines 10 and 29) IS THE ONE NAME NO INDEPENDENT
!     SOURCE CONFIRMS.  Neither revision of C22-6728 mentions it,
!     and the only volume-OCR hits are this page's own two cards
!     (OCR lines 7851 and 7870), which are the same ink read by a
!     worse reader and are NOT a witness.  It rests on (a) FORK
!     being English where FCRK is not, (b) the page's own
!     "LCCATICN" calibration, and (c) the two printed instances
!     agreeing with each other.  Recorded as UNRESOLVED-BY-A-
!     SECOND-SOURCE; see WHAT COULD NOT BE SETTLED.
!
! (3) "Z EVL MK" (line 7) is likewise not in the manual, but its
!     DEFINING card is on another printed page and the volume OCR
!     reads it there: "221152.00  003004.00+   ? EVL MK  VF,
!     (8)3004.  -$RD MASK - SEL,VER,CONSOLE" (OCR line 9397), with
!     the next card at 221152.40 being "E MK1A VF,(8)3000. -$ AND
!     SWEF MASK".  The manual independently names EMK1A as a thing
!     that gets loaded "in SEVLMK", which is precisely what line 8
!     does with Z EVL MK.  The Z prefix is the module's, shared
!     with Z START, Z STEVL and Z DISK 1, all three typeset-
!     confirmed.
!
! (4) THE BYTES THAT LOOKED DOUBTFUL WERE SETTLED ON WHAT PRODUCED
!     THEM, not on ink:
!     * line  9's second word reads ".36 F0" at 1800 dpi with a
!       closed 0; the assembler produces F0, and printed p.18
!       prints "CM1111(BU,1)" six times, every one "001000.36 F0".
!     * line 48's second word prints "000000.C1 0C" -- the ".C1"
!       is an impossible octal C, so that row IS dropping ink on
!       round glyphs, and the byte's open second glyph is a
!       damaged 0.  The statement settles it outright: the
!       assembler emits "000000.01 00" for "RD,0.0($14),0".
!     * line 33's "217567.72 C0" and line 44's "217572.41 D0" look
!       like the same confusion and are NOT: both are produced
!       exactly as printed.  The D of D0 has the straight vertical
!       left stem and squared corners that a C and a 0 do not.
!
! (5) THE COMMENT COLUMN, used as the oracle it is:
!     * line 39's "-IF IOD NULL, USE LABEL MODE" prints the middle
!       letter as the broken-right round shape.  IOD is the term
!       (cf. printed p.84's "T IODK  -THE IOD COUNT"); ICD is not.
!     * line 13's "-ILLEGAL EQUIP CODE - FAKE EPGK" is recorded
!       verbatim.  EPGK is read off the ink with a clean G
!       crossbar and is NOT an English word; nothing on this page
!       or in the manuals explains it, and it is a COMMENT, so
!       nothing depends on it.
!
! (6) MNEMONICS: "KVI" (line 32) and "LVI" (lines 7, 10) are the
!     K/L pair, not an O/C or B/8 confusion, and both are real
!     operations, so the assembler-as-eliminator test is silent
!     here by construction.  What decides it is the printed bits:
!     the 6-bit field after the "." carries the index register as
!     bits 19-22, so both spellings print the same ADDRESS and
!     differ only in the operation byte.  MEASURED, at this
!     page's own SLC, varying nothing else:
!
!       KVI,4,4.0  ->  000004.11 04
!       LVI,4,4.0  ->  000004.11 01
!
!     The page prints 04.  (Note what this is NOT: K and L are not
!     one of this drum's confusable pairs, so the reading was
!     never in real doubt; the measurement is recorded because the
!     claim was made.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LABELS PRINTED WITH BLANKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "Z START", "K FORK", "K TEST M", "K YOME", "K GO", "B IRA",
! "B CWCR", "Z EVL MK", "S EVL MK", "S EVL TB", "S CH OP",
! "K ILEGL", "Z DISK 1", "Z STEVL", "K K LOC", "R VFY", "P CSRD",
! "S FILE K", "S SCRPM", "RS1 FLK", "S F MODE", "S LABM",
! "K K MODE", "K MODE", "S CW ADR" and "S IO INS" all print with
! blanks and are written closed up, as every deck since p.2 does
! -- the deck format takes a label to the first blank.  Each is
! six characters or fewer closed up (C22-6531 printed p.10).  The
! typeset manual prints them ALREADY closed up (ZSTART, KYOME,
! RS1FLK, KKLOC, ...), which is an independent witness that the
! closed-up form is the name and not an artifact of this format.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE TWO ASTERISKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every line number carries an asterisk after it ("5*", "48*").
! That is the ordinary column.  TWO lines carry a SECOND asterisk
! after the LOCATION: line 26 (217557.00) and line 48 (217572.00).
! This is the unexplained marker of docs/listing_typography.md 12.
! What this page ADDS to the record: p.144's marker fell on its
! SLC line and on a full word at an odd half word; here the SLC
! line (line 4) is NOT marked, and line 26 is an ordinary half-
! word "B,K ILEGL" at an EVEN half word, byte-for-byte identical
! to the fourteen other B,K ILEGL rows around it, none of which is
! marked.  So neither "the SLC is marked" nor "an odd half word is
! marked" survives this page.  Recorded as open, with nothing
! added to it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- every one pinned by a card on a DIFFERENT page
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ZERO TAUTOLOGICAL ROWS.  This page's own cards sit at OCR lines
! ~7840-7887 of docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt; every witness
! cited below is at a different OCR line and a different printed
! page, or in a typeset manual.
!
! The nine unit-area field offsets are all carried by LANDED decks
! at these same values, and this page's printed bits agree with
! every one of them to the BIT (a VFL offset is printed in full in
! the 6-bit field, modulo the half-word/index packing noted under
! GLYPHS (6)) -- which is nine independent joins between this page
! and pp.99/101/102, none of them arranged by me.
SEVLTB  SYN(BU,19), 2.0      ! p.101 line 11 "S EVL TB SYN(BU,19),2.0"
SEVLMK  SYN(BU,19), 2.32     ! p.101 line 12 "S EVL MK SYN(BU,19),2.32"
SCWADR  SYN(BU,18), 3.32     ! p.101 line 14 -CONTROL WORD ADDRESS
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0      ! p.101 line 17 -IO INSTR. LAST
SSCRPM  SYN(BU,64), 6.0      ! p.101 line 20 -SCRATCH PAD MEMORY
SLABM   SYN(BU,2),  7.16     ! p.101 line 22 -MODE SPECIFIED IN
SFILEK  SYN(BU,12), 7.38     ! p.101 line 25 -FILE COUNT
SFMODE  SYN(BU,2),  2.48     ! p.102 line 13 -FILE MODE
SCHOP   SYN(BU,1),  0.26     ! p.99  line 22 -CHAN OPERATING
! The eleven code externals.  Each printed address below is read
! off THIS page's BINARY OUTPUT column; the NAME and the fact that
! a card defines that address are from elsewhere, as cited.
! B 1RA    221140.00  >>> CORRECTED 2026-10-31: THIS WAS "B IRA",
!                     LETTER I, AND THE MANUAL CITATION DID NOT
!                     HOLD. <<<  The two revisions print the SAME
!                     SENTENCE both ways --
!                       C22-6728   "BIRA; B, BCWCR, with the..."
!                       C22-6728-1 "B1RA; B, BCWCR, with the..."
!                     -- so quoting one of them was selective.  And
!                     that OCR shares the drum's 1/I confusion: it
!                     renders RS1FLK as "RSIFLK" seven times against
!                     one correct "RS1FLK", and THIS DECK took the
!                     DIGIT there.  Rung 2 of the glyph ladder does
!                     not fire on the 1/I pair.
!
!                     SETTLED ON THE INK, in one row, three
!                     characters apart.  Line 5 prints
!                     "Z START  SIC,B 1RA" and at 1800 dpi the I of
!                     SIC has a SYMMETRIC top bar extending equally
!                     left and right; the glyph after "B " has a
!                     flag at the TOP LEFT ONLY and no right
!                     extension.  That is the drum's digit 1.
!                     printed p.153 found this and rendered both
!                     pages; re-rendered here before changing it.
!
!                     NO BIT MOVES -- the SYN is to a literal either
!                     way -- and check_symbol_spellings could never
!                     have caught it: 1/I was not in its CONFUSABLE
!                     set until this correction added it.
B1RA    SYN, (8)221140.0
! B CWCR   221102.00  same manual sentence; the DEFINING card is
!                     on another printed page: volume OCR
!                     "221102.00 = 221133.01 CO BB CWO RR
!                     SVASCJPICK ACER OF CWE", i.e. a card at
!                     221102.00 whose statement is an SVA to
!                     J PICK.  THE OCR'S NAME FIELD IS GARBLED
!                     THERE; the spelling is the manual's.
BCWCR   SYN, (8)221102.0
! Z EVL MK 221152.00  defining card on another printed page,
!                     volume OCR "221152.CC CC3004.0C+ 2 CVL MK
!                     VF,(8)3004. $RD MASK - SEL,VER,CONSG", i.e.
!                     a VF card at 221152.00 holding (8)3004 with
!                     a read-mask comment.  The OCR's name is
!                     garbled; the reading Z EVL MK is THIS page's
!                     own line 7, corroborated only by the Z
!                     prefix and by what line 8 does with it.
ZEVLMK  SYN, (8)221152.0
! K ILEGL  220064.00  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p127.strap already SYNs
!                     KILEGL at (8)220064.0, citing printed p.160
!                     (PDF 167) where the label card is printed.
KILEGL  SYN, (8)220064.0
! Z DISK 1 217577.00  defining card on another printed page,
!                     volume OCR "217577.00 215C01.21 80
!                     217601.34 O02 ZUISKL BB,SLOCSU,$+2.0" -- a
!                     card at 217577.00 whose name the OCR garbles
!                     to ZUISKL.  ZDISK1 is typeset in C22-6728,
!                     three times in each revision.
ZDISK1  SYN, (8)217577.0
! Z STEVL  221144.40  the status evaluation entry, named in type
!                     by C22-6728 ("It is entered at ZSTEVL").
!                     Pinned to the half word by a card on
!                     another printed page, volume OCR
!                     "220065.4C 221144.63 C1 ... DZ STEVE":
!                     an LVI at 220065.40 naming 221144, and 0o63
!                     is 0o40 plus LVI's index bits, so the
!                     half-word select bit IS on -- which is why
!                     this deck writes .40 and not .0.
ZSTEVL  SYN, (8)221144.40
! K K LOC  220065.40  that same card, at 220065.40 on a
!                     different printed page, is K K LOC's
!                     defining card; the OCR garbles its name
!                     field, and KKLOC is typeset in C22-6728
!                     fourteen times.
KKLOC   SYN, (8)220065.40
! R VFY    221161.00  defining card on another printed page,
!                     volume OCR "221161.CO COCCO7.31 BC
!                     221165474 02 R VEY B8BS SYSTM($12),R RR
!                     TEST IF SYSTEM TAPE" -- a card at 221161.00
!                     testing S SYSTM.  The OCR reads the name
!                     "R VEY"; RVFY is typeset in C22-6728.
RVFY    SYN, (8)221161.0
! P CSRD   217071.00  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p138.strap DEFINES the
!                     label PCSRD at 217071.00 (its line 21,
!                     "PCSRD LV,$1,S UNA($10)").  Typeset as
!                     PCSRD in C22-6728.
PCSRD   SYN, (8)217071.0
! RS1 FLK  220143.00  defining card on another printed page,
!                     volume OCR "220143.00  000007.31 8C
!                     220174.74 00  RS1 FLK  BZB,S SYSTM($12),
!                     K N SYST".  Typeset as RS1FLK.
RS1FLK  SYN, (8)220143.0
! K K MODE 217624.40  defining card on another printed page,
!                     volume OCR "217624.40 217624.5C CO K K MUDE
!                     6,4" -- a card AT 217624.40 (so the .40 half
!                     word is right), name OCR'd as K K MUDE.
!                     Another printed page carries the identical
!                     "SIC,K K MODE" -> 217624.40 80.  KKMODE is
!                     typeset in both revisions of C22-6728.
KKMODE  SYN, (8)217624.40
! K MODE   217615.00  defining card on another printed page,
!                     the OCR of the defining page is too garbled
!                     to read its name ("217615.CC 1. C3 30 KK
!                     MECE SV HE"), but the ADDRESS is there and
!                     TWO other printed pages print "B,K MODE"
!                     -> 217615.10 00 (volume OCR lines 8008 and
!                     9435; line 7882 is this page's own card and
!                     is NOT counted).  KMODE is typeset in
!                     C22-6728 as "CHECK FOR PROPER MODE
!                     SELECTED".
KMODE   SYN, (8)217615.0

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN.  The page prints "SLC,$" (line 4, at 217544.00).
! Restated hard so the deck assembles standalone; see THE JOIN.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)217544.0

! ---- the READ routine --------------------------------------------
ZSTART  SIC,B1RA                     ! line  5
        B,BCWCR                      ! line  6  -BRANCH TO CHECK CW
        LVI,8,ZEVLMK                 ! line  7
        SV,8,SEVLMK($12)             ! line  8  -STORE MASK ADDR IN UA
