! Line 48 is a FULL word, so the counter reaches 217573.00 for
! whatever page follows.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THESE CHECKS DO AND DO NOT ESTABLISH
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All forty-four emitting statements are declared -- forty-six
! half words -- and all five of the page's own labels.  Nothing on
! this page is left unchecked and nothing was substituted: every
! statement below is the PRINTED form, with blanks closed up in
! labels per the deck format, and strap_asm accepted every one.
!
! THE REAL CHECKS OF THIS PAGE'S OWN COUNTING are the six rows
! whose operand is a label defined HERE:
!   line 10  LVI,8,K FORK  -> 217560.61, and K FORK is line 29
!   line 16  B,K TEST M    -> 217565.10, and K TEST M is line 38
!   line 33  BZXE,K YOME   -> 217567.72, and K YOME is line 43
!   line 35  BZXVZ,K TEST M-> 217565.31, same target, different op
!   line 44  SVA,0,K GO+.32-> 217572.41, and K GO is line 48
!   line 46  LX,0,$+1.0    -> 217572.00, which is K GO's location
! Four of them are FORWARD references nineteen, twenty-two, ten
! and four rows ahead, so each one only resolves if every
! intervening row's LENGTH is right.
!
! A SEVENTH, INDEPENDENT CHECK OF THE SAME COUNTING: line 44's
! "K GO+.32" and line 46's "$+1.0" both name 217572.00 by two
! DIFFERENT routes -- one through the label, one through the
! location counter -- and the two printed words agree.
!
! TAUTOLOGY AUDIT: none.  Every external is defined by a card on
! another printed page or by a landed deck, cited under EXTERNALS.
!
! WHAT IS PINNED ONLY TO THE HALF WORD, from this page alone: the
!   eleven code externals.  A branch, a SIC and an LVI all print
!   only bit 18 of the address (the half-word select), bits 19-22
!   being the index register, so bit offsets 0-31 encode
!   identically and ".00" is a CONVENTION there, not a reading
!   (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "AN EXTERNAL BACK-DERIVED
!   FROM A BRANCH OR AN LVI").  Z STEVL and K K LOC are written
!   ".40" and K K MODE ".40" because that bit IS checked and
!   writing ".0" would fail.  Each name's own defining card is
!   cited above.
! WHAT IS PINNED TO THE BIT from this page: the nine unit-area
!   offsets, whose VFL 6-bit field carries the full offset --
!   S CH OP at 0.26 prints "000000.32" outright on line 9, and
!   S EVL MK (2.32), S LABM (7.16), S FILE K (7.38), S F MODE
!   (2.48) and S CW ADR (3.32) each print a byte that changes if
!   the offset moves.  All nine agree with pp.99/101/102.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT COULD NOT BE SETTLED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) "K FORK" HAS NO SECOND READER.  Neither revision of C22-6728
!     mentions it, and the volume OCR's only two hits are this
!     page's own lines 10 and 29 -- same ink, worse reader, not a
!     witness.  C22-6728's Figure 90, which charts this exact
!     routine box by box and names fifteen of its symbols, has NO
!     K FORK box: the equipment-table dispatch is drawn as
!     decision diamonds, so the label never appears.  Z EVL MK is
!     absent from that figure for the same reason.  The name rests on FORK being English, on the
!     page's own "LCCATICN" calibration, and on the two printed
!     instances agreeing.  NOTHING ON THIS PAGE DEPENDS ON THE
!     SPELLING: K FORK is a label defined and referenced only
!     here, so every !CHECK passes either way.  That is exactly
!     the class of error docs/transcription_workflow.md says the
!     oracle is blind to.  If a later page turns out to reference
!     it, that reference is the check this deck cannot supply.
!
! (b) "Z EVL MK" (line 7) likewise.  Its defining card IS on
!     another printed page at 221152.00, and the OCR of that card
!     fixes the ADDRESS and the VF datum, but garbles the NAME.
!     Z EVL MK is this page's reading alone.  Same blindness: the
!     address is checked, the spelling is not.
!
! (c) THE SECOND ASTERISK on lines 26 and 48 is unexplained, and
!     this page kills two readings of it (see THE TWO ASTERISKS).
!
! (d) "FAKE EPGK" (line 13's comment).  Read off clean ink with a
!     plain G crossbar, not an English word, and not found in
!     either manual or anywhere else in the volume OCR.  It is a
!     comment, so nothing depends on it, but it is not understood.
!
! (e) WHY THE HEADING'S LOCATION FIELD IS BLANK HERE.  Measured
!     blank, not guessed.  Why some pages print it is still open.
!
! (f) THE BIT OFFSETS OF THE ELEVEN CODE EXTERNALS, below bit 32.
!     Branches, SIC and LVI print only the half-word select, so
!     ".00"/".40" is as fine as this page can see; each name's
!     defining card elsewhere is cited under EXTERNALS, but this
!     deck did not re-render those pages.
!
! (g) WHY lines 5 and 6 are TWO cards when the other three
!     statement pairs on this page share one.  Printed, not
!     explained.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER LIMITATION HIT: none.
! No printed spelling was rejected by strap_asm.  Accepted exactly
! as printed: "SIC,B IRA" and its branch (an intra-page SIC/branch
! pair, so the p.131 straddle problem does not arise), the
! connective "CM1111(BU,1)", the entry-mode-free index forms
! "($4)", "($10)", "($12)", "($13)", "($14)", the self-relative
! "$+1.0", the label-relative "K GO+.32", "CNOP", and "SLC,$" --
! which assembles, and is restated hard here only so the deck
! stands alone; see THE JOIN for what that costs.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

!SYM   ZSTART   217544.00
!SYM   KFORK    217560.40
!SYM   KTESTM   217565.00
!SYM   KYOME    217567.40
!SYM   KGO      217572.00
